he damage they did to the wealthy  resort city Yoda trolls Luke Star Wars  fans hungry for some original trilogy  nostalgia were probably pleased by the  fact that practical puppetry effects  were used for Yoda's force ghost  appearance and Frank Oz also returned to  voice the character also returning to  the last Jedi was Yoda's trademark  quirky sense of humor a Yoda quite  unlike the serious Jedi Mass  you're seen in the prequel movies Yoda  surprises both Luke and the audience by  calling down lightning to strike the  tree containing the Jedi Order texts we  later learned that Rey stole the ancient  Jedi texts and hid them aboard the  Millennium Falcon but Luke doesn't know  that Yoda is just doing what he did back  on Dagobah teasing Luke for the fun of  it  Luke trolls kylo Luke's final scenes in  the last Jedi were among the best in the  entire film after mysteriously appearing  on crates Luke has a short visit with  his sister Leia before walking out alone  on the salt plane to confront his nephew  Luke toys with kylo giving Leia and the  others time to escape after promising to  haunt kylo and telling him that he will  not be the last Jedi the truth is  revealed Luke has been using the force  to project an image of himself across  the galaxy back on his secluded Island  Luke passes away peacefully from the  massive effort presumably becoming one  with the force and while these scenes  represent the best of the last Jedi  there are plenty of moments that may  have made the audience cringe Skye  walking one of the most surprising  moments of the last Jedi was when Leia  uses the force to pull herself back  through space to the damaged resistance  flagship we've never seen Leia use the  force like that at least not in a movie  it's long been known that she has the  same potential power as her twin brother  Luke  so the concept itself didn't come out of  the blue what really made this one of  the worst moments of the last Jedi was  the way it was executed with 